{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793493371,"nonce":"3+/gtScyMCTutp44RVtniH35rGM=","title":"macOS llvm-backend executables load Homebrew's libzstd at launch","message":"zylua and zypy built with `llvm-backend` on macOS link `/opt/homebrew/opt/zstd/lib/libzstd.1.dylib`: llvm-config lists `-lzstd` among LLVM's system libraries, and llvm-sys adds `/opt/homebrew/lib` to the search path, where ld takes the dylib over the archive beside it. The dylib is outside the shared cache, so every launch maps, validates and binds it, and the executable does not start on a Mac without Homebrew's zstd (the CI release builds included).\n\nCost, Mac, a C program linking it against one without: +2.7M instructions before main, about 0.2 ms. zylua print(1) before main: 24.6M instructions with the dylib, 22.2M with the archive.","files":null}]}